messages:
maria: Quick pass on the rules editor UI — two UX pain points: reordering feels jumpy on long lists, and the validation pill reads "Invalid order" which is pretty vague. Screenshot attached :mag:. Thoughts?

devon: For long lists, virtualize height and show a ghost placeholder while dragging. Items snapping feels jarring. Use transform-based movement and will-change: transform for perf. Also honor prefers-reduced-motion so folks with motion sensitivity get instant snap.

sam: About the validation copy: options I like are "Rule conflict — prerequisites required" or "Disabled: unmet prerequisites". Both are more actionable. We should add a micro-CTA in the popover: "Show affected rules".

kate: A11y notes: keyboard reorder needs focus management + an aria-live region (polite) announcing both from/to positions: e.g., "Moved 'Block suspicious IPs' from 4 to 2". Make sure the drag handle is a single tab stop and set aria-grabbed on grab. Color can't be the only disabled indicator.

leah: I'll mock two popover CTA variants: "Show dependencies" and "Auto-fix suggestions". For auto-fix we should show a confirmation modal that lists changes before applying.

sam: Quick contrast check on the screenshot: disabled text at 50% opacity fails WCAG for 12px text on #0f1724. Need ~4.5:1. Recommend using #6B7280 at full opacity for small text or keep lighter color but add a subtle pill background for the label. I'll run axe and post ratios later today.

devon: Animation snippet that worked in my prototype: 
```css
.rule-row {
  transition: transform 140ms cubic-bezier(.22,.9,0,1);
  will-change: transform;
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .rule-row { transition: none; }
}
```
This keeps motion smooth but respects reduced-motion. Also add a small slide on drop so destination is visible.

maria: For the preview simulation, let's add a compact timeline that shows pre/post order and a toggle "Simulate changes". When filters are applied, label it "Effective order". If the system auto-inserts a fallback rule, show a toast explaining why and link to the auto-fix flow.

deploy-bot: Preview deployed to staging: https://staging.redwood.com/routing/editor/canary

maria: Great. Schedule a 15m walkthrough tomorrow 09:30am to cover: a11y verification (contrast + live announcements), microcopy variants, and reduced-motion behavior. Please bring screenshots or recordings of the prototype.
